    "created_at": "2018-01-25T12:46:34Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-01-25T12:46:34Z",
    "body": "```html\r\n<script>\r\ndocument.removeChild(document.documentElement);\r\nnewRoot = document.appendChild(document.createElement(\"x\"));\r\nnewBody = newRoot.appendChild(document.createElement(\"body\"));\r\ndocument.bgColor = \"black\"\r\nw(newBody.bgColor)\r\n</script>\r\n```\r\nin https://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/ yields the empty string in Chrome and Firefox, and black in Edge and Safari.\r\n\r\nSo aligning the getter seems reasonable, but it seems we should do that by changing \"the body element\" concept, provided someone does more exhaustive analysis.",
